# Shell scripts MUST keep LF line endings — they execute on the Linux GCP VM
# (e.g. scripts/db/migrate.sh, scripts/create_kafka_topics.sh, cd-gcp.yml steps).
# A CRLF shebang fails with "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash\r". The repo had
# no .gitattributes and relied on each developer's core.autocrlf; this makes the
# line ending deterministic regardless of the checkout platform.
*.sh text eol=lf

# SQL init/migration files are read by psql inside the postgres container; keep
# them LF for byte-stable behaviour and to silence autocrlf normalisation churn.
*.sql text eol=lf

# The committed B-prime record (uplift/bprime_record.py) is pinned by the sha256 of its EXACT
# bytes: the CI artifact as uplift.yml run 36860454801 wrote it. A checkout that rewrote its
# trailing LF as CRLF (core.autocrlf on Windows) would change that digest and refuse the record
# on that machine alone, so no line-ending conversion is applied to it anywhere.
docs/state/bprime/*.json -text

# The committed Power_Report (uplift/power.py) is the controls' CI artifact, committed unedited
# from uplift.yml run 41268743674; the same rule keeps its bytes exact on every checkout.
docs/state/uplift-power-report.json -text
